 sh4: return to the main loop after a delay slot that starts a TB

`rte` ends its TB before the delay slot (DISAS_STOP), so the slot runs in a
TB of its own that is entered from the main loop.  That loop's interrupt
check runs first, and superh_cpu_exec_interrupt declines a HARD interrupt
in a delay slot ("Delay slots are indivisible"); the TB-exit request is
consumed with it.  The slot TB then chained with lookup_and_goto_ptr, so a
source that stays asserted with no new edge (the kick only fires on
edges) was never taken while the guest sat in a self-linked idle TB.

The SH-4 accepts a pending interrupt as soon as the rte delay slot
completes, so a TB that started in a delay slot now exits to the main
loop after it.

--- a/target/sh4/translate.c
+++ b/target/sh4/translate.c
@@ -262,7 +262,12 @@
            delayed jump as immediate jump are conditinal jumps */
         tcg_gen_mov_i32(cpu_pc, cpu_delayed_pc);
         tcg_gen_discard_i32(cpu_delayed_pc);
-        if (use_exit_tb(ctx)) {
+        /*
+         * Exit to the main loop after a TB that started inside a
+         * delay slot, so an interrupt still pending at the new IMASK is
+         * taken, as the SH-4 does after rte.
+         */
+        if (use_exit_tb(ctx) || (ctx->tbflags & TB_FLAG_DELAY_SLOT_MASK)) {
             tcg_gen_exit_tb(NULL, 0);
         } else {
             tcg_gen_lookup_and_goto_ptr();
